<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Admirable Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Congreso Admirable</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Admirable Congress was the constituent congress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia that met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> from January to May 1830, presided over by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a>. It drafted a new constitution and accepted the resignation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> as president. Venezuela had already broken away, and Ecuador soon followed, so its constitution never governed the whole union.</p></div>
